{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_36d3adddb1c1512f5da3cd83283c196217521694e3075cc544a3bc78429f0993"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Installation is via Claude Code plugin marketplace commands: '/plugin marketplace add 2389-research/claude-plugins' followed by '/plugin install binary-re@2389-research'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5fc43892852603f17cd786b50be6fff722d04b80118e640a1d1863e552eded77"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The stated philosophy is that the LLM drives analysis while the human provides context: the user supplies platform, hardware, theories, and constraints, and Claude runs tools, forms hypotheses, and designs experiments."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9c886225fbed3bab1747bdb8ad8417e4a35fca5eb14b483119b64816ccff7cb1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Required external tools include radare2, qemu-user, and gdb-multiarch installed via apt, plus frida-tools via pip and ARM hard-float/arm64 cross sysroot packages (libc6-armhf-cross, libc6-arm64-cross)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9d44c3cf6906aad16366cfc5e077b1295f4e0242f31e3bea36d3be2f73a5c5be"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The example interaction shows the skill recording facts, stating a hypothesis with a confidence score of 0.7, then asking the user whether to proceed with static analysis or dynamic analysis under QEMU."},{"claim_ids":["clm_db1dc933e9900f1bd3d50f0946ee0369a125a3731bcbd64642929293e9648ce0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plugin ships a 'binary-re' skill described as a structured RE workflow with hypothesis-driven analysis, driven by hypothesis-testing rather than blind exploration."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e7295b2093cdf142c0d288f5b9d22d7ff5129dd115d4a4f6ef6559afb4f0c6dc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Stated use cases include firmware analysis, protocol reverse engineering, security research on embedded systems, and hardware hacking of robot/IoT device internals."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f5ec2725684eae24f606cc5f01f3ba2624d8f1baf909c7af4ed5d1dc79d90437"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The skill asks for confirmation before executing binaries (even sandboxed), network-capable dynamic analysis, operations requiring device access, and major changes in analysis direction."}],"claim_ids":["clm_36d3adddb1c1512f5da3cd83283c196217521694e3075cc544a3bc78429f0993","clm_5fc43892852603f17cd786b50be6fff722d04b80118e640a1d1863e552eded77","clm_9c886225fbed3bab1747bdb8ad8417e4a35fca5eb14b483119b64816ccff7cb1","clm_9d44c3cf6906aad16366cfc5e077b1295f4e0242f31e3bea36d3be2f73a5c5be","clm_db1dc933e9900f1bd3d50f0946ee0369a125a3731bcbd64642929293e9648ce0","clm_e7295b2093cdf142c0d288f5b9d22d7ff5129dd115d4a4f6ef6559afb4f0c6dc","clm_f5ec2725684eae24f606cc5f01f3ba2624d8f1baf909c7af4ed5d1dc79d90437"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:28:43Z","created_by_operation":"op_e53f2004bc444b618f87e9a14e2680e0","id":"pg_f89d58d6477a5c908b081482bb7d05b5","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/2389-research-binary-re-readme-md-42aee9063f3f-1482bb7d05b5.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_da3c62d57db655ed8a4b5d3fc51e7811"],"title":"2389-research/binary-re/README.md @ 42aee9063f3f","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:28:43Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e53f2004bc444b618f87e9a14e2680e0"}
